To whom it may concern,

A 62-year-old patient contacted our pharmacy after developing a mild rash on
her forearms approximately three days after starting Atorvastatin 20 mg
Tablets dispensed from batch ATV-250902 (manufactured 2 September 2025,
expiry 30 September 2027). She reports taking one tablet daily as prescribed.
The rash is non-blistering and she has not required medical treatment so far,
but she has stopped taking the medication.

We have advised the patient to contact her physician. The batch comprised
5000 packs; this is the first complaint received for it. The patient purchased
one pack (30 tablets) and has retained the remaining tablets and packaging.

Please advise on the next steps, including whether a formal adverse event
report should be filed.

